<card id="c" title="What&apos;s on My Raspberry Pi 5">
<do type="prev" label="Back"><prev/></do>
<p>For easy switching between movies, I quickly assembled a solution in the form of a one-pager based on <b><a href="https://www.airtable.com/">airtable</a></b>, <b><a href="https://airtable.com/developers/web/api/introduction">airtable API</a>,</b> <b>js</b> and <a href="https://www.omdbapi.com/">Omdbapi API</a>, so when adding a link to the movie and its title in the table, the poster and description are automatically loaded and displayed on the home page of Chromium on the Raspberry when opened.</p>
<p>In addition, the Raspberry Pi 5 has Bluetooth, making it easy to connect to an audio system.</p>
<p>In the end, it turns into a media solution for watching movies and listening to music while also running the services.</p>
<p>How do you use your Raspberry Pi?</p>
